
* How to create branch, merge branches, stash & git reset?

{Branch}

Commands-

- git branch                                   (To see list of available branches)
- git branch <New branch name>                 (Create a new branch)
- git checkout <name of branch you want to go> (To switch branch)
- git branch -d                                (Delete a branch)
- git branch -D                                (Delete a branch)

# The "-d" option will delete the branch only, If it has already pushed or merged with remote branch.
# Use "-D" if you want t force to deleted, If it has not pushed or merged yet.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{Merge}


* You can't merge branches of diff Repo             [mumbai.git <---MERGE---> mumbai.git]
* We use pulling mechanism to merge branches        [mumbai.git <---can't MERGE---> singapore.git]


Commands-

- git merge <branch name>     (To merge the branch)
- git log                     (To verify the merge)
- git push origin master      (To push to central repo like github)


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{Conflict}

* When same name file having different content in different branches, if you do merge, conflict occurs. (Resolve conflict then Add & Commit)
* Conflict occurs when you merge Branches.

#Ex:-


    MASTER                         Branch1                                |         Master                                  Branch
    ------                         -------                                          ------                                  ------
    File1                          File2                                  |         File1                                   File2

 - My name is chandan        - My name is chandan                         |   - My name is chandan		      - I am a trainer
                             - I am a trainer

     <------ Merge Successful --------->                                  |           <----------- CONFLICT Occours ------------->
                                                                          | 
									  |   * When file1 & file2 have completely different then conflict occurs.


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{Git Stash}

* Suppose you are implementing a new feature for your product. Your code is in progress and Suddenly a customer escalation comes, Because of this, You have to keep aside your new featire work for few hours.
* To stash an item (only applies to modified files not new files) 


Commands-


- git stash                                                                  (To stash an item)
- git stash list                                                             (To see stashed items list)
- git stash apply stash@{0}   #---> {0} <--- latest stashed file             (To apply stashed items)
                                    {1}
                                    {2}
                                    {3}



* Then you can add & commit


- git stash clear                                                            (To clear the stash items)


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{Git Reset}


* Git reset is a powerful command that is used to undo local changes to the state of a git repo. (Delete all the code from the staging are)

* To reset staging area ---->  # git reset <File-name>
                               
                               # git reset .       ( . --> Means If anything in the file then Reset or Remove all)



* To reset the changes from both staging area and working directory at a time --->  # git reset --hard
                                                              
                                                                                   (Delete the code from both Staging area and Working directory)





